schema: public-use-boundary
object:
  title: Boundary — chamas/iqqub/hawala attribution in inclusive-practices.md
  tier: public-with-caveat
  consent_note: >-
    inclusive-practices.md references chamas (Kenya), iqqub (Ethiopia and
    Eritrea), and hawala networks as evidence that community-designed
    financial systems already serve people banks refuse. This is a
    broad-strokes, secondary-source reference to whole national/regional
    practices, not sourced to a specific community, operator, or
    citation. Do not present as an authoritative or complete account of these
    systems; seek community-sourced or specialist review before republishing
    in a context that speaks on behalf of the communities that run them.
  review_type: domain-review-before-public-use
  notes: >-
    Covers the concept-lineage entry "Informal community savings mechanisms
    (chamas, iqqub, hawala)" and the accompanying claim-evidence entry (same
    work order) — flagged per the ingest skill's community/cultural-
    attribution high-risk trigger.
  ai_assisted: true
  provenance:
    origin: src/content/docs/inclusive-practices.md
    transformation: synthesized
    authorship: ai-assisted
